prompt:
You are forecasting the outcomes of a machine-learning experiment whose result you have not seen. Give
calibrated probabilities.

Experiment:
This experiment trains two LoRA adapters on Qwen3-8B-Base: one on a corpus of documents stating claims plainly and one on the same task with a false note. Each adapter receives 50 training updates. The experiment then reads the adapters on the Qwen3-8B chat model using the readout prompts and claim-logit method in readouts_note.json. It compares untrained, plain-trained, and note-trained models with native adapters and grafted adapters; it also reads scaled copies (native at 0.5× and grafted at 2×). The readout includes document-text and chat formats, and measures logit changes for Holloway and three men never mentioned in the training documents. For each arm, compute Holloway-specific excess L as Holloway’s logit change minus the corresponding change for the three strangers. The note’s share of plain’s excess L is the note arm’s excess L divided by the plain arm’s excess L, computed separately for each format. Report both arms’ excess L as well as the share. Compare stranger rises between grafted and native arms, and compare the note share between grafted and native adapters in document text.

Questions:
[
 {
  "qid": "q1",
  "question": "Does grafted plain retain enough Holloway-specific excess L to read the share?",
  "labels": {
   "pass": "Grafted plain L is at least half native plain L in both formats.",
   "gate failed": "Grafted plain L is under half native plain L in both formats; also check at 2\u00d7 scale."
  }
 },
 {
  "qid": "q2",
  "question": "Are strangers\u2019 rises smaller under graft than native?",
  "labels": {
   "both formats": "Strangers\u2019 rise is smaller under graft than native in both formats.",
   "not both formats": "Strangers\u2019 rise is not smaller under graft than native in at least one format."
  }
 },
 {
  "qid": "q3",
  "question": "Is grafted note\u2019s share at least 0.2 below native note\u2019s share in document text?",
  "labels": {
   "yes": "Grafted note share is at least 0.2 below native note share.",
   "no": "Grafted note share is less than 0.2 below native note share."
  }
 }
]

Answer with JSON only: {"forecasts": [{"qid": "q1", "probabilities": {"<label>": <p>, ...}}, ...]}
Each question's probabilities must cover exactly its labels and sum to 1.
